arm64: support ACPI-only EFI boot with a stub FDT

Keep the flattened tree services required by the EFI stub while allowing an
ACPI-only arm64 kernel to omit the runtime Open Firmware device-tree core.
Provide the small core and header stubs needed by that supported Kconfig
state.

This overlay-created compatibility patch is deliberately limited to the
common arm64/OF boundary.  It omits unrelated 32-bit ARM, Xilinx, platform
compile-coverage, and generic GIC cleanups.  The optional numbered 10010
patch may be omitted; the base kernel remains buildable without file-based
kexec.

